<title>LEBANON: LEBANON TRADE DEFICIT WIDENS IN H1 TO $3.18 BLN.</title>
<headline>LEBANON TRADE DEFICIT WIDENS IN H1 TO $3.18 BLN.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's trade deficit for the first six months of 1997 rose to $3,178 million from $3,023 in the same period of 1996, according to customs figures released on Thursday.</p>
<p>The June deficit fell to $505 million from $600 million in May and was unchanged compared to June of 1996.</p>
<p>The High Customs Council issued the following figures (in millions of dollars):</p>
<p>MERCHANDISE TRADE</p>
<p>			     June97    May97    Apr97     Mar97</p>
<p>Monthly Exports		51	 49	 47	  69</p>
<p>Imports			 556	649	639	 615</p>
<p>Trade balance year-to-date </p>
<p>Exports			 368	317	268	 220</p>
<p>Imports		     3,546    2,990    2,341     1,702</p>
<p>Balance		    -3,178   -2,673   -2,073    -1,482</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (9611) 645307  745308  602057</p>
